---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Terminal UI"
  description="The Veasel Code TUI is SolidJS + OpenTUI: mint chrome, pixel splash, Compose, Ctrl+P command palette, reviews, and / @ $ autocomplete."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / TUI</p>
    <h1>
      The terminal UI
      <br />
      <em>worth standardizing on.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The terminal client is <strong>SolidJS + OpenTUI</strong> — Veasel mint
      chrome, pixel splash, a Compose panel, <kbd>Ctrl+P</kbd> command palette,
      review overlays, and <code>/</code> · <code>@</code> · <code>$</code>{" "}
      autocomplete — talking to the local loopback API. Multiline drafts, live +
      completed MarkdownRenderable replies, DiffRenderable reviews with content
      washes, mode-aware context footers, dedicated system/tool theme tokens,
      custom JSON themes, and reduced-motion mode. Type <code>/help</code> in a
      session for the live shortcut list.
    </p>

    <div class="compatibility-banner">
      <span class="compatibility-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        ⌘
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>
          SolidJS + OpenTUI · mint · Ctrl+P · reviews · / @ $ autocomplete
        </strong>
        <p>
          Veasel-branded shell (not OpenCode) · pixel splash on home · Compose
          with Shift+Enter newlines · <kbd>Ctrl+P</kbd> command palette ·{" "}
          <kbd>Ctrl+R</kbd> pending reviews · <kbd>$</kbd> skills / fuzzy{" "}
          <kbd>@</kbd> paths / slash suggestions · <kbd>v</kbd> DiffRenderable
          with content washes · Markdown for the latest live and completed turn
          · context footers by mode · builtin + project/user JSON themes
          (system/tool tokens) · <code>VEASEL_TUI_REDUCED_MOTION</code> keeps
          busy glyphs static · status uses ● idle / ◌ busy / ▲ attention / ✖
          error without inventing progress bars.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Home and sessions</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>k</kbd> or arrows move the session list;{" "}
          <kbd>g</kbd> / <kbd>G</kbd> jump first/last when no filter is active;{" "}
          <kbd>1</kbd>–<kbd>9</kbd> open the Nth visible session (sidebar labels
          those slots); Enter opens; <kbd>n</kbd> starts a session when the list
          is empty.
        </li>
        <li>
          Type to filter by title or directory. <kbd>Ctrl+L</kbd> or Esc clears
          the filter; the status line states which match is focused. Home/End
          and PgUp/PgDn page long lists. Selection stays on screen with a plain{" "}
          <code>Selected N of M</code> cue.
        </li>
        <li>
          Esc cancels a running turn (it never clears the composer). Session
          history and events live in local SQLite.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Compose, palette, and transcript</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Architecture:</strong> the client is SolidJS on{" "}
          <code>@opentui/solid</code> / <code>@opentui/core</code>. Product
          chrome stays Veasel mint; the original pixel companion is the home
          identity cue and is distributed under the project MIT license.
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Ctrl+P</kbd> opens the command palette (Ctrl+K stays kill-line in
          Compose). <kbd>Ctrl+R</kbd> jumps to pending reviews;{" "}
          <kbd>Ctrl+G</kbd> toggles the latest activity group when present.
        </li>
        <li>
          With an empty Compose panel, <kbd>↑</kbd> / <kbd>↓</kbd> recall
          earlier submissions. PgUp/PgDn page the transcript; Home/End jump
          edges. End sticks to the latest reply while streaming.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Multiline drafts:</strong> <kbd>Enter</kbd> submits.{" "}
          <kbd>Shift+Enter</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl+J</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl+Enter</kbd>, or{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+Enter</kbd> insert a newline (OpenTUI <code>Textarea</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Type <kbd>@</kbd> to autocomplete workspace paths under the session
          directory (<kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Enter</kbd> inserts; Esc dismisses).
          Ranking is typo-tolerant: exact / prefix / substring first, then
          one-edit fuzzy matches.
        </li>
        <li>
          Type <kbd>$</kbd> to autocomplete discovered Skills as a one-shot{" "}
          <code>$source/skill</code> token (same Tab/Enter/Esc keys;
          typo-tolerant ranking). This inserts a mention for the turn — it does
          not replace <code>/skill on</code> for lasting session enablement.
        </li>
        <li>
          Readline edits: <kbd>Ctrl+A</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+E</kbd> ends,{" "}
          <kbd>Ctrl+←</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+→</kbd> or <kbd>Alt+B</kbd> /{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+F</kbd> by word, <kbd>Ctrl+U</kbd> clear draft,{" "}
          <kbd>Ctrl+W</kbd> or <kbd>Alt+Backspace</kbd> delete previous word,{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+D</kbd> delete forward through the next word,{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+C</kbd> capitalize the next word, <kbd>Alt+U</kbd> /{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+L</kbd> upcase / downcase the next word, <kbd>Ctrl+K</kbd>{" "}
          kill to end, <kbd>Ctrl+T</kbd> transpose characters around the cursor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Ctrl+Y</kbd> copies the latest assistant reply (OSC 52). Esc
          dismisses a notice or review first; a second Esc returns home. Esc
          also cancels an in-flight turn — it never clears the composer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>MarkdownRenderable:</strong> while stick-to-bottom follows the
          latest assistant body, live streaming and the completed turn both
          render through OpenTUI <code>MarkdownRenderable</code> (themed markup
          + fenced code). Scrolling earlier lines falls back to TextChunk
          markdown tones so Home/PgUp still page history; End remounts Markdown
          for the latest reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          Transcript chrome tones fenced-code language tags, blockquotes, and
          muted diff context separately; add/remove diff lines use bold chrome.
          Truncated review summaries say how many lines remain (and{" "}
          <code>{"}"}</code> when more hunks exist). Role labels keep dedicated{" "}
          <code>system</code> / <code>tool</code> theme tokens so hierarchy
          stays readable beside assistant/user colors.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Context footers:</strong> the always-visible footer swaps by
          mode — default discovery, <code>@</code>-path / <code>$</code>-skill /
          slash completion keys, pending-review hotkeys, or Esc cancel · End
          follow while streaming — so the row stays under ~72 columns without
          stuffing every hotkey at once.
        </li>
        <li>
          Status uses ● idle, ◌ busy, ▲ attention, and ✖ error. Idle shows the
          active provider/model when configured. Busy grows from{" "}
          <code>thinking…</code> to measured <code>streaming · N chars</code>.
          While scrolled above a live stream, the cue reads{" "}
          <code>streaming below · End follows</code>; End restores follow.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reduced motion:</strong> set{" "}
          <code>VEASEL_TUI_REDUCED_MOTION=1</code> (or GTK{" "}
          <code>gtk-enable-animations=false</code>) to keep the busy glyph and
          streaming cursor static instead of blinking.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Credentials and models</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <code>/connect</code> — paste an API key, save it locally, pick a
          model (happy path). Provider lists support the same j/k · g/G · 1–9 ·
          type-to-filter · Ctrl+L keys.
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>s</kbd> or <code>/models</code> — full settings: endpoint
          (Ctrl+U), output budget (Ctrl+O), and model discovery.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keys are stored under{" "}
          <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/model-settings.json</code> with owner-only
          POSIX permissions (plaintext at rest). Saved profile keys win over
          environment variables for the same provider.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Themes</h2>
      <p>
        Use <code>/theme</code> to list and switch themes. Builtins:{" "}
        <code>mint</code> (default product look), <code>ember</code>,{" "}
        <code>slate</code>, <code>mono</code>, <code>aurora</code>,{" "}
        <code>day</code> (light), and <code>contrast</code> (high-contrast
        light). The choice is stored in <code>~/.config/veasel/tui-theme</code>{" "}
        (override with <code>VEASEL_TUI_THEME</code>). While the{" "}
        <code>/theme</code> menu is open, ↑/↓ preview colors live; Enter keeps
        the choice and Esc restores the saved theme.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Custom JSON themes:</strong> drop <code>*.json</code> files
        under <code>~/.config/veasel/themes/</code> or{" "}
        <code>&lt;workspace&gt;/.veasel/themes/</code>. Each file needs{" "}
        <code>id</code>, <code>name</code>, and optional <code>extends</code> (a
        builtin id) plus hex color overrides — including dedicated{" "}
        <code>systemLabel</code> / <code>systemText</code> /{" "}
        <code>toolLabel</code> / <code>toolText</code> tokens.{" "}
        <code>/theme</code> lists those directories (missing, empty, or with
        filenames) and surfaces clear errors for bad JSON. Project themes
        override user themes with the same id; builtins cannot be replaced.
      </p>
      <pre><code
        >{`{
  "id": "ocean",
  "name": "Ocean",
  "description": "Deep blue workspace",
  "extends": "mint",
  "brand": "#7dd3fc",
  "shellBg": "#0a1628",
  "systemLabel": "#7dd3fc",
  "toolLabel": "#e6c07b"
}`}</code
      ></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Reviews and slash commands</h2>
      <p>
        Type <code>/</code> for suggestions. Common flows:
      </p>
      <pre><code>/patches
Ctrl+R   # select a patch to inspect and approve/reject

/commands
Ctrl+R   # inspect and approve/reject a shell command

veasel mcp add [user|project] stdio &lt;name&gt; &lt;command&gt; [args…]
veasel mcp add [user|project] http &lt;name&gt; &lt;url&gt;
veasel mcp enable|disable|remove [user|project] &lt;name&gt;
veasel mcp credentials … · veasel mcp oauth …
/mcp   # browse configured and session-trusted servers
/mcp trust configured/&lt;name&gt;
/mcp calls or Ctrl+R   # inspect and approve/reject a tool call

/skills [filter]
/skill on|off &lt;name&gt;
/plugin add|remove &lt;path&gt;
/map
/usage</code></pre>
      <p>
        File edits, shell, and MCP never take effect until you inspect and
        approve. Open the unified review panel with <code>Ctrl+R</code> (or the
        matching <code>/patches</code>, <code>/commands</code>, or{" "}
        <code>/mcp calls</code> command), then select a pending item:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <kbd>Space</kbd> multi-select · <kbd>a</kbd> / <kbd>x</kbd> approve or
          reject the selection (or current item)
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Shift+A</kbd> / <kbd>Shift+X</kbd> approve or reject all pending
          of that kind
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>{"{"}</kbd> / <kbd>{"}"}</kbd> move between diff hunks ·{" "}
          <kbd>]</kbd> / <kbd>[</kbd> or <kbd>n</kbd> / <kbd>p</kbd> move
          between pending reviews
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>v</kbd> toggles OpenTUI DiffRenderable split view (synced scroll,
          themed +/- signs, separate gutter/content washes, selection colors,
          filetype SyntaxStyle) without leaving the review
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Ctrl+R</kbd> opens the first pending review list (patches,
          commands, or MCP calls)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Configured MCP persists in user <code>mcp-servers.json</code> or project{" "}
        <code>.veasel/mcp-servers.json</code>; workspace <code>.mcp.json</code>{" "}
        imports read-only. Trust is still per-session. OAuth:{" "}
        <code>veasel mcp oauth authorize|complete|refresh</code> — refresh uses
        a stored refresh token when present. Token values are never shown.
        Prefer headless <code>veasel mcp oauth … --listen</code> when Veasel
        should own the loopback listener (it still does not open a browser). See
        the <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Fresh on main — landing in the next verified release</h2>
      <p>
        These terminal improvements are merged on <code>main</code> and ship
        with the next verified prerelease; the current verified channel tag is
        in the site footer.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Drafts survive restarts.</strong> Pending composer text and
          attachments are kept per session in a local state file (0600), so
          closing the TUI no longer loses a half-written prompt.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>API keys never render.</strong> The key prompt masks every
          character — the secret never reaches the terminal buffer or a captured
          frame.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Real Markdown replies.</strong> Assistant messages and
          streaming render headings, lists, tables, and syntax-highlighted code
          fences; role labels stay readable without color.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cursor-aware completion.</strong> Moving back into an{" "}
          <code>@</code> path or <code>$</code> skill mention reopens its menu
          and completing keeps the text after the mention.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Approvals require inspection.</strong> Review details load
          when you open an item; batch approval stays blocked until every target
          was actually shown.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reduced motion honored.</strong> The streaming cursor goes
          static when <code>VEASEL_TUI_REDUCED_MOTION</code> or the OS asks for
          less motion.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Forks and attention</h2>
      <p>
        <code>/fork</code> copies the current session's chat history into a new
        session (title suffixed “ (fork)”) and switches to it, so you can try a
        different direction without losing the original thread. Usage and tool
        state stay with the source session. When the terminal window is not
        focused, a finished or failed turn raises a desktop notification;
        focused terminals stay quiet and rely on the status line.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Usage and cost honesty</h2>
      <p>
        <code>/usage</code> shows provider-reported token totals, average per
        reported turn, and optional cache counters when adapters set{" "}
        <code>usage.reported</code>. USD cost appears only when every reported
        turn matches the pinned schedule — otherwise unavailable. Veasel does
        not invent cost figures, % cache savings, or Harbor Index scores.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        Configure providers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/skills/`}>
        Skills and plugins <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>
        MCP servers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
